prs.body:
I've been doing some profiling of ssr rendering, and noticed that `guardReactiveProps` had a presence.

most of that came from render-function components passing their setup context `attrs` straight through, which is very common in headless UI libraries (reka-ui's `Primitive` alone was 164 instances per request of my ~690 component page):

```ts
setup(props, { attrs, slots }) {
  return () => h(props.as, attrs, { default: slots.default })
}
```

`attrs` here is a `Proxy`, and the `Object.assign` we end up doing by default adds ~2µs per copy for objects with only a handful of keys.

so this PR lets `guardReactiveProps` read the raw attrs object through the proxy via a private symbol and copy that instead.

on the Nuxt page this made `GET /` about ~5% faster. in isolation:

| | before | after | delta |
| - | - | - | - |
| `renderToString`, 200 components doing `h('div', attrs)` (prod cjs) | 710µs | 388µs | -45% |
| client mount + unmount, same tree (prod cjs) | 939µs | 597µs | -36% |

